18. NextRAD: Real-Time Precipitation WMS
WMS Tiles are pre-rendered map images from a server. Here we use NOAA/NEXRAD weather radar (Iowa Mesonet Program):

conus = filter(us_states(), !stusps %in% c("AK", "PR", "HI"))

leaflet() |&gt; 
  addProviderTiles(providers$CartoDB) |&gt; 
  addPolygons(data = st_union(conus), fillColor = "transparent",
              color = "black", weight = 1) |&gt; 
  addWMSTiles(
    "http://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/cgi-bin/wms/nexrad/n0r.cgi",
    layers = "nexrad-n0r-900913",
    options = WMSTileOptions(format = "image/png", transparent = TRUE)
  )

Why WMS? Real-time data (precipitation, radar), pre-rendered, responsive on mobile, server handles rendering.

